  "assumptions": [
    {
      "what": "Equal split between the paired TDs: the B-edge reaction of band 2-3 (533.4 lb) goes half to TD1 (pulled through the strut, tension at 2B) and half to TD2 (pushed, compression at 3B), 266.7 lb each.",
      "why": "Book assumption (p1, p5); an engineer input, not statics."
    },
    {
      "what": "Load: 200 plf per ft of depth over A-B and 173.33 plf over B-C. At each depth the load is shared by the sheathed bands in proportion to width over the full 150 ft: band 1-2 20 plf, band 2-3 26.67 plf, band 3-5 153.33 plf (B-C: 20 and 153.33 only). Total 9733 lb.",
      "why": "Book p2-p3 gives section loads only; seismic load proportional to diaphragm width."
    },
    {
      "what": "Line A walls share R_A in proportion to length (76.52 plf on SW1 and SW2). Line C walls each take their own band reaction plus the TD reaction at C (SW3 713.36 lb, SW4 4046.3 lb), not a length split.",
      "why": "Book p7. Line C is broken between 2 and 3, so each piece must close on its own."
    },
    {
      "what": "Sign convention: the \"+\" element in this example (top face +x, bottom -x, left face -y, right face +y; \"positive direction\" arrow to the left) is the mirror of the Ex 4.1 element. Printed unit-shear signs already follow it, so no conversion is applied. Member forces are tension +.",
      "why": "FORMAT.md: book sign per the figure element. A tool using the Ex 4.1 element must negate every unit shear in this file."
    },
    {
      "what": "Book section names A, B, C mean bands 1-2, 2-3, 3-5; keys here use grid names only.",
      "why": "Section names clash with grid names."
    },
    {
